# Line-ending policy.
#
# Everything is normalized to LF in the repository AND checked out as LF, including on
# Windows. This matters beyond tidiness: Git Bash refuses to run a script whose shebang
# ends in CR (`#!/usr/bin/env bash^M` -> "bad interpreter: No such file or directory"),
# so any shell script or git hook checked out with CRLF is silently broken. Declaring the
# policy up front is far cheaper than diagnosing it later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the two categories that actually break when they get CRLF.
*.sh   text eol=lf
hooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
